Ryujinx shader translator: when a global address is the sum of two constant-buffer values, GlobalToStorage preferred the
second one, so "c[1][0x20] + c[0][0x40]" (an offset from the shader's constant data plus the storage descriptor) became a
storage buffer bound from c[1]. A c[0] (driver reserved) addend is now preferred over one from another bank. The Ryujinx
code in the context lines is MIT.
Also: an access no descriptor can be traced for is resolved at run time instead of being dropped: the storage descriptors of the stage the runtime marks (the Lichii emulator's fallback), then the guest page table (AmpereGlobal.cs).

